; vulkanBlendProof.pi4 - exact Vulkan source-over acceptance scene.
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. IT DOES NOT SHIP. This is the blend-enabled variant of the
; two-pass Vulkan triangle proof. It uses only public Vulkan entry points and
; asks for exactly the one blend equation Anvil accepts:
;
;   color/alpha op: ADD
;   source factor:  SRC_ALPHA
;   dest factor:    ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA
;   write mask:     RGBA
;   logic op:       disabled
;
; Both passes clear to opaque blue. Pass one draws half-alpha red and must
; read back purple ($BF80007F); pass two draws half-alpha green after its own
; clear and must read back teal ($BF00807F). These are V3D's complementary
; 128/255 and 127/255 UNORM factors. Outside samples must remain blue
; ($FF0000FF). Thus disabled blending, swapped factors, a missing master bit,
; or an inherited disabled-path blend mask cannot satisfy the pixel oracle.
;
; The normal triangle proof remains the disabled-blend control. This wrapper
; deliberately shares its full guard, V3D-job, BCL-viewport, fence, pixel and
; teardown oracle instead of growing a second copy that could drift.
;
; Desk build:
;   PureMetalForge.exe --compile \
;       RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/vulkanBlendProof.pi4 -t pi4 \
;       --load-addr 0x500000 --stack-addr 0x4F00000 --entry-returns \
;       -o vulkanBlendProof.img
;
; Visual acceptance on a future explicitly authorized board run: a solid
; teal triangle on blue, held for six seconds. The returned 64-word report is
; laid out exactly as vulkanTriangleProof.pi4; slots 1 and 4 must both be zero,
; slots 14..16 must be FF0000FF, BF80007F, BF00807F, and slot 47 must be one.

#VTP_BLEND_PROOF = 1
#VTP_LIST_PROOF = 0
#VTP_INDEXED_PROOF = 0
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/vulkanTriangleProofBody.pbi"
